# Model Routing & Efficiency Rules

**Last Updated:** 2026-05-19
**Purpose:** Cost-efficient model routing with 3-tier escalation: Ollama → Haiku → Codex

---

## The Golden Rule

> **Always start with Ollama. Escalate only when necessary. Never skip directly to Codex unless explicitly instructed or failure threshold is reached.**

---

## Model Selection Matrix

| Tier | Alias | Full Path | Use For | Cost |
|------|-------|-----------|---------|------|
| **1. Default** | `ollama` | `ollama/kimi-k2.5:cloud` | Intent classification, simple edits, file nav, summarization, boilerplate, linting explanations, low-risk/repetitive tasks | FREE |
| **2. Escalate** | `haiku` | `anthropic/claude-3-haiku-20240307` | Ollama uncertain/low-confidence, API integrations, multi-file moderate logic, better reasoning needed (cost/speed still matters) | $0.25/1M |
| **3. Max** | `gpt` / `GPT` | `openai/gpt-5.4` / `openai/gpt-5.1-codex` | Haiku fails or is uncertain, debugging requires multiple attempts, architecture/system reasoning, large refactors, unclear test failures, terminal/tool execution, explicit "use Codex" or "max intelligence" | ~$3/1M |

**⚠️ IMPORTANT:** Aliases (`gpt`, `haiku`) work in main session but **FAIL in subagents**. Use **full model paths** in `sessions_spawn()`. See Subagent Model Paths section below.

**Key Update:** Kimi-K2.5 is competitive with paid models for most tasks. Haiku fills the gap between free Ollama and expensive Codex for moderate complexity coding.

